kosha transition-metals-varga

  -- d-block elements: Sc through Zn, and the rows below.
  -- what makes transition metals special: partially filled d-orbitals.
  -- this gives them:
  --   variable valence:    Fe²⁺/Fe³⁺, Cu⁺/Cu²⁺, Mn²⁺/Mn⁴⁺/Mn⁷⁺ etc.
  --   coloured compounds:  d-d electron transitions absorb visible light
  --                        Fe²⁺ = pale green, Fe³⁺ = orange, Cu²⁺ = blue
  --   catalytic activity:  partially filled d-orbitals bind substrates
  --                        Fe in haemoglobin, Cu in cytochrome c oxidase
  --   magnetic properties: unpaired d-electrons → paramagnetism, ferromagnetism
  --                        Fe, Co, Ni are ferromagnetic at room temperature
  -- most important industrial metals are here: Fe, Cu, Zn, Ti, Ni, Cr, Mn.

  "metals-varga-vishesa"
  "chemistry-varga-vishesa"

  "d-orbital-swarupa variable-valence-yukta"
  "coloured-compound-swarupa catalytic-swarupa"
  "magnetic-yukta"
  "iron-drishthanta copper-drishthanta zinc-drishthanta"

